        "Content": "3 BED   2 BATH   DETACHED PERIOD HOUSE   OFCH   149sqm   MATURE GARDENS   ORIGINAL FEATURES.\r\nNB: SEE VIRTUAL TOUR\r\n\r\nA Distinguished Detached Period Residence (Protected Structure) in the Heart of Coastal Skerries\r\nHogan Estates are delighted to present Station House, a charming and character-filled 3-bedroom, 2-bathroom detached period residence extending to approximately 149 sq.m. (1,604 sq.ft.), ideally positioned on Station Road in the heart of the highly sought-after coastal town of Skerries.\r\n\r\nThis exceptional home offers a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial detached residence that effortlessly combines period elegance with everyday comfort. Rich in original architectural features and boasting generously proportioned accommodation throughout, Station House retains the timeless charm and character synonymous with homes of this era.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from oil-fired central heating, mature landscaped gardens providing excellent privacy, a large detached garage, and ample off-street parking, making it an ideal family home in one of North Dublin's most desirable residential locations.\r\n\r\nAccommodation & Features\r\n•\tDetached period residence\r\n•\tApprox. 149 sq.m. (1,604 sq.ft.)\r\n•\t3 spacious bedrooms\r\n•\t2 bathrooms\r\n•\tOil-fired central heating\r\n•\tNumerous original period features\r\n•\tMature private gardens\r\n•\tLarge detached garage\r\n•\tExcellent off-street parking\r\n•\tPrime town-centre location\r\n•\tWalking distance to rail, beach and amenities\r\n•\tOutstanding Coastal Location\r\n\r\nStation House enjoys an enviable location within walking distance of the vibrant seaside town of Skerries, renowned for its beautiful beaches, harbour, coastal walks, excellent schools and exceptional community spirit.\r\n\r\nEducation\r\nFamilies are exceptionally well catered for, with a range of highly regarded schools nearby including:\r\n•\tSt Patrick's Junior School\r\n•\tSt Patrick's Senior School\r\n•\tHolmpatrick National School\r\n•\tSkerries Educate Together National School\r\n•\tArdgillan Community College\r\n•\tA selection of Montessori and childcare facilities throughout the town.\r\n\r\nSporting & Recreational Amenities\r\nSkerries is renowned for its strong sporting tradition and offers an impressive array of clubs and facilities including:\r\nGAA\r\nSkerries Harps GAA Club, one of Fingal's most respected clubs with thriving football, hurling and camogie sections.\r\nSoccer\r\nSkerries Town FC, catering for boys, girls and adult teams with excellent facilities.\r\nRugby\r\nSkerries RFC, established in 1926 and a cornerstone of sporting life in North County Dublin.\r\nGolf\r\nSkerries Golf Club, a renowned 18-hole championship parkland course established in 1905 and enjoying spectacular coastal views.\r\nAdditional Sporting Facilities\r\n•\tSkerries Hockey Club\r\n•\tThe Hills Cricket Club\r\n•\tSailing, swimming and watersports facilities\r\n•\tTennis clubs and fitness centres\r\n•\tExtensive coastal walking routes and beaches.\r\n•\tRetail & Lifestyle Amenities\r\n\r\nResidents benefit from an excellent range of local services and retail facilities, including:\r\n•\tSuperValu Skerries\r\n•\tLidl\r\n•\tIndependent boutiques and speciality shops\r\n•\tCafés, artisan bakeries and delicatessens\r\n•\tAward-winning restaurants, pubs and waterfront dining\r\n•\tPharmacies, medical services and professional practices\r\n•\tNearby shopping destinations in Swords, Pavilions Shopping Centre, and Balbriggan.\r\n\r\nThe town centre offers an attractive mix of local businesses and national retailers, all contributing to Skerries' unique village atmosphere.\r\n\r\nCultural & Community Amenities\r\nSkerries is one of Dublin's most vibrant coastal communities and offers a wealth of cultural and heritage attractions including:\r\n•\tSkerries Library\r\n•\tSkerries Community Centre\r\n•\tSkerries Mills, one of Ireland's most significant milling complexes\r\n•\tSkerries Historical Society\r\n•\tLocal arts, music and community festivals\r\n•\tCoastal heritage walks and harbour amenities.\r\n\r\nExcellent Transport Links\r\nStation House is exceptionally well connected for commuters.\r\nRail\r\nSkerries Train Station is within walking distance.\r\nFrequent commuter rail services operate to Dublin Connolly Station with journey times of approximately 35 minutes.\r\nRegular services also connect to Balbriggan, Drogheda, Dundalk and Belfast.\r\nBus\r\nThe area is served by the Dublin Bus Route 33, providing direct access to Dublin City Centre and numerous intermediate destinations.\r\nRoad Network\r\nConvenient access to the M1 Motorway\r\nExcellent connectivity to the M50\r\nEasy access to the Dublin Port Tunnel\r\nApprox. 20-25 minutes to Dublin Airport depending on traffic conditions.\r\n\r\nA Rare Opportunity\r\nProperties of this calibre and character rarely come to the market in such a prestigious and convenient location. Offering generous accommodation, original period features, mature gardens and exceptional access to Skerries' outstanding amenities, Station House represents a unique opportunity to acquire a truly special family home.\r\n\r\nEmail Hogan Estates TODAY to arrange a viewing. Don’t miss this rare opportunity to snap up a truly exceptional home."
